<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex122.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{\omega}\sim\mathcal{D}}\nabla_{\theta_{i}}J(\theta(k),\boldsymbol{\omega})=\nabla_{\theta_{i}}\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{\omega}\sim\mathcal{D}}J(\theta(k),\boldsymbol{\omega})=\nabla_{\theta_{i}}J(\theta(k))." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{\omega}\sim\mathcal{D}}\nabla_{\theta_{i}}J(\theta(k),\boldsymbol{\omega})=\nabla_{\theta_{i}}\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{\omega}\sim\mathcal{D}}J(\theta(k),\boldsymbol{\omega})=\nabla_{\theta_{i}}J(\theta(k)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma13" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 13</span></span><span id="Thmlemma13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma13.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma13.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The following holds almost surely,</p>
<table id="A7.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex123"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex123.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max(" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max(</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex123.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\hat{g}(k)\|,\|g(k)\|,\|h(k)\|,\|\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta(k),\hat{\mathcal{D}}^{M})\|,\|\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta(k),\mathcal{D}^{M})\|,\|\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta(k))\|)\leq\frac{\bar{r}L}{(1-\gamma)^{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>M</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>M</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\hat{g}(k)\|,\|g(k)\|,\|h(k)\|,\|\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta(k),\hat{\mathcal{D}}^{M})\|,\|\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta(k),\mathcal{D}^{M})\|,\|\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta(k))\|)\leq\frac{\bar{r}L}{(1-\gamma)^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">We decompose the error between <math id="A7.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{g}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{g}(k)</annotation></semantics></math> and the true gradient as follows</span></p>
<table id="A7.E12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A7.E12X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E12X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{g}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{g}(k)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E12X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\underbrace{\hat{g}(k)-g(k)}_{e^{1}(k)}+\underbrace{g(k)-h(k)}_{e^{2}(k)}+\underbrace{h(k)-\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta(k),\hat{\mathcal{D}}^{M})}_{e^{3}(k)}+\underbrace{\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta(k),\hat{\mathcal{D}}^{M})-\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta(k),\mathcal{D}^{M})}_{e^{4}(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>M</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>M</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>M</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\underbrace{\hat{g}(k)-g(k)}_{e^{1}(k)}+\underbrace{g(k)-h(k)}_{e^{2}(k)}+\underbrace{h(k)-\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta(k),\hat{\mathcal{D}}^{M})}_{e^{3}(k)}+\underbrace{\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta(k),\hat{\mathcal{D}}^{M})-\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta(k),\mathcal{D}^{M})}_{e^{4}(k)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A7.E12Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E12Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\underbrace{\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta(k),\mathcal{D}^{M})-\nabla_{\theta_{i}}J(\theta(k),\mathcal{D})}_{e^{5}(k)}+\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta(k))." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>M</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\underbrace{\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta(k),\mathcal{D}^{M})-\nabla_{\theta_{i}}J(\theta(k),\mathcal{D})}_{e^{5}(k)}+\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta(k)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS3.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">We will bound each term separately and combine these bounds to prove Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3 (Policy gradient convergence, informal). ‣ Actor convergence. ‣ 6.1 Convergence ‣ 6 Convergence results and adaptation gap ‣ Causality Meets Locality: Provably Generalizable and Scalable Policy Learning for Networked Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Bounds on <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{1}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{1}(k)</annotation></semantics></math>.</h5>

<div id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The following lemmas follows similar steps as in the proof <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma14" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 14</span></span><span id="Thmlemma14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Lemma 14, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite>)<span id="Thmlemma14.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma14.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma14.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="Thmlemma14.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is large enough s.t.</p>
<table id="A7.Ex124" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex124.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{C_{a}\left(\tfrac{\delta}{2nM},T\right)}{\sqrt{T+t_{0}}}+\frac{C^{\prime}_{a}}{T+t_{0}}\leq\frac{2c\rho^{\kappa+1}}{(1-\gamma)^{2}},\quad\text{where}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>where</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{C_{a}\left(\tfrac{\delta}{2nM},T\right)}{\sqrt{T+t_{0}}}+\frac{C^{\prime}_{a}}{T+t_{0}}\leq\frac{2c\rho^{\kappa+1}}{(1-\gamma)^{2}},\quad\text{where}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A7.Ex125" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex125.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{a}(\delta,T)=\frac{6\bar{\epsilon}}{1-\sqrt{\gamma}}\sqrt{\frac{\tau h}{\sigma}}\left[\log\left(\frac{2\tau T^{2}}{\delta}\right)+f(\kappa)\log SA\right],\quad C^{\prime}_{a}=\frac{2}{1-\sqrt{\gamma}}\max\left(\frac{16\bar{\epsilon}h\tau}{\sigma},\,\frac{2\bar{r}}{1-\gamma}(\tau+t_{0})\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mi>γ</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mi>σ</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>δ</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mi>γ</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mi>σ</mi></mfrac><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{a}(\delta,T)=\frac{6\bar{\epsilon}}{1-\sqrt{\gamma}}\sqrt{\frac{\tau h}{\sigma}}\left[\log\left(\frac{2\tau T^{2}}{\delta}\right)+f(\kappa)\log SA\right],\quad C^{\prime}_{a}=\frac{2}{1-\sqrt{\gamma}}\max\left(\frac{16\bar{\epsilon}h\tau}{\sigma},\,\frac{2\bar{r}}{1-\gamma}(\tau+t_{0})\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma14.p1.2" class="ltx_p">with <math id="Thmlemma14.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\epsilon}=4\tfrac{\bar{r}}{1-\gamma}+2\bar{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\epsilon}=4\tfrac{\bar{r}}{1-\gamma}+2\bar{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, then we have with probability at least <math id="Thmlemma14.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\tfrac{\delta}{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\tfrac{\delta}{4}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A7.Ex126" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex126.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{0\leq k\leq K-1}\|e^{1}(k)\|\leq\frac{4cL\rho^{\kappa+1}}{(1-\gamma)^{3}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{0\leq k\leq K-1}\|e^{1}(k)\|\leq\frac{4cL\rho^{\kappa+1}}{(1-\gamma)^{3}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Bounds on <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{2}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{2}(k)</annotation></semantics></math>.</h5>

<div id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> be the <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra generated by the trajectories in the first <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> outer-loop iterations. In particular, let <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> be the <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra generated the trajectories in the first phase of Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 4.3 Key idea: meta-learning via actor-critic optimization ‣ 4 Generalizable and scalable actor-critic ‣ Causality Meets Locality: Provably Generalizable and Scalable Policy Learning for Networked Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. Note that <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\boldsymbol{\omega}^{1:M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝝎</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\omega}^{1:M}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\hat{\boldsymbol{\omega}}^{1:M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\boldsymbol{\omega}}^{1:M}</annotation></semantics></math> are <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>-measurable. In addition, <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta(k)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math>-measurable, and so is <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{i}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{i}(k)</annotation></semantics></math>. Further, by the way that the trajectory <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(s(t),a(t))\}_{t=0}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(s(t),a(t))\}_{t=0}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> is generated, we have <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[g(k)|\mathcal{G}_{k-1}]=h(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[g(k)|\mathcal{G}_{k-1}]=h(k)</annotation></semantics></math>. As such, <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{k}\langle\nabla J(\theta(k)),e^{2}(k)\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{k}\langle\nabla J(\theta(k)),e^{2}(k)\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> is a martingale difference sequence w.r.t. <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, and we have the following bound which is a direct consequence of Azuma-Hoeffding bound.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma15" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 15</span></span><span id="Thmlemma15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Adapted Lemma 15 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite>)<span id="Thmlemma15.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma15.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma15.p1.1" class="ltx_p">With probability at least <math id="Thmlemma15.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta/4</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A7.Ex127" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex127.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}\langle\nabla J(\theta(k)),e^{2}(k)\rangle\right|\leq\frac{2\bar{r}^{2}L^{2}}{(1-\gamma)^{4}}\sqrt{2\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}^{2}\log\frac{8}{\delta}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}\langle\nabla J(\theta(k)),e^{2}(k)\rangle\right|\leq\frac{2\bar{r}^{2}L^{2}}{(1-\gamma)^{4}}\sqrt{2\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}^{2}\log\frac{8}{\delta}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Bounds on <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{3}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{3}(k)</annotation></semantics></math>.</h5>

<div id="Thmlemma16" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 16</span></span><span id="Thmlemma16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Adapted Lemma 16, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite>)<span id="Thmlemma16.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma16.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma16.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="Thmlemma16.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T+1\geq\dfrac{\log\left(\dfrac{c(1-\gamma)}{\bar{r}}\right)+(\kappa+1)\log\rho}{\log\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T+1\geq\dfrac{\log\left(\dfrac{c(1-\gamma)}{\bar{r}}\right)+(\kappa+1)\log\rho}{\log\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have almost surely,</p>
<table id="A7.Ex128" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex128.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|e^{3}(k)\|\leq 2\dfrac{Lc}{(1-\gamma)}\rho^{\kappa+1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|e^{3}(k)\|\leq 2\dfrac{Lc}{(1-\gamma)}\rho^{\kappa+1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Bounds on <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{4}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{4}(k)</annotation></semantics></math>.</h5>

<div id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Since the error between <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\boldsymbol{\omega}}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\boldsymbol{\omega}}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\omega}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝝎</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\omega}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded as <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\hat{\boldsymbol{\omega}}^{m}-\boldsymbol{\omega}^{m}\|_{2}\leq\delta_{\boldsymbol{\omega}}(T_{e})=C_{\boldsymbol{\omega}}\sqrt{\frac{\log(n/\delta)}{T_{e}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝝎</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>𝝎</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>𝝎</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\hat{\boldsymbol{\omega}}^{m}-\boldsymbol{\omega}^{m}\|_{2}\leq\delta_{\boldsymbol{\omega}}(T_{e})=C_{\boldsymbol{\omega}}\sqrt{\frac{\log(n/\delta)}{T_{e}}}</annotation></semantics></math> with probability at least <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>. Using Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption5" title="Assumption 5. ‣ 6.1 Convergence ‣ 6 Convergence results and adaptation gap ‣ Causality Meets Locality: Provably Generalizable and Scalable Policy Learning for Networked Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> (iii), we have with probability at least <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta/4</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A7.E13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A7.E13X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E13X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\forall k,e^{4}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\forall k,e^{4}(k)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E13X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta(k),\hat{\mathcal{D}}^{M})-\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta(k),\mathcal{D}^{M})\leq L_{J}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\frac{1}{M}\|\hat{\boldsymbol{\omega}}^{m}-\boldsymbol{\omega}^{m}\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>M</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>M</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝝎</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta(k),\hat{\mathcal{D}}^{M})-\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta(k),\mathcal{D}^{M})\leq L_{J}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\frac{1}{M}\|\hat{\boldsymbol{\omega}}^{m}-\boldsymbol{\omega}^{m}\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A7.E13Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E13Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq L_{J}C_{\boldsymbol{\omega}}\sqrt{\frac{\log(4nM/\delta)}{T_{e}}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>𝝎</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq L_{J}C_{\boldsymbol{\omega}}\sqrt{\frac{\log(4nM/\delta)}{T_{e}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Bounds on <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{5}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{5}(k)</annotation></semantics></math>.</h5>

<div id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first state the uniform concentration bound for vector-valued functions.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma17" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 17</span></span><span id="Thmlemma17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma17.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma17.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="Thmlemma17.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{1},x_{2},\ldots,x_{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{1},x_{2},\ldots,x_{M})</annotation></semantics></math> be i.i.d. samples from a distribution <math id="Thmlemma17.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="Thmlemma17.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="Thmlemma17.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta\subset\mathbb{R}^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta\subset\mathbb{R}^{p}</annotation></semantics></math>, and consider <math id="Thmlemma17.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathcal{X}\times\Theta\to\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathcal{X}\times\Theta\to\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> with the following properties: (i) For all <math id="Thmlemma17.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=1,\ldots,d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=1,\ldots,d</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmlemma17.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|f_{j}(x,\theta)|\leq B\ \text{for all }(x,\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|f_{j}(x,\theta)|\leq B\ \text{for all }(x,\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>; (ii) For all <math id="Thmlemma17.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma17.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=1,\ldots,d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=1,\ldots,d</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmlemma17.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|f_{j}(x,\theta)-f_{j}(x,\theta^{\prime})|\leq L\cdot\|\theta-\theta^{\prime}\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|f_{j}(x,\theta)-f_{j}(x,\theta^{\prime})|\leq L\cdot\|\theta-\theta^{\prime}\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, with probability at least <math id="Thmlemma17.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta/4</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A7.Ex129" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex129.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{\theta\in\Theta}\left\|\frac{1}{M}\sum_{i=1}^{M}f(x_{i},\theta)-\mathbb{E}[f(X,\theta)]\right\|_{2}=\mathcal{O}\left((B+L)\sqrt{\frac{dp\log M+\log(4/\delta)}{M}}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>M</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{\theta\in\Theta}\left\|\frac{1}{M}\sum_{i=1}^{M}f(x_{i},\theta)-\mathbb{E}[f(X,\theta)]\right\|_{2}=\mathcal{O}\left((B+L)\sqrt{\frac{dp\log M+\log(4/\delta)}{M}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma17.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the hidden constant is universal.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Observe that for <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta,\mathcal{D}^{M})\right]=\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>M</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta,\mathcal{D}^{M})\right]=\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>. Using Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma17" title="Lemma 17. ‣ Bounds on 𝑒^5⁢(𝑘). ‣ G.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix G Missing proofs in Section ‣ Causality Meets Locality: Provably Generalizable and Scalable Policy Learning for Networked Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>, we have with probability at least <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta/4</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A7.E14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A7.E14X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E14X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sup_{k}\left\lVert e^{5}(k)\right\rVert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mi>k</mi></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sup_{k}\left\lVert e^{5}(k)\right\rVert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E14X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sup_{k,\theta\in\Theta}\left\lVert\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta,\mathcal{D}^{M})-\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta)\right\rVert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>M</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sup_{k,\theta\in\Theta}\left\lVert\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta,\mathcal{D}^{M})-\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta)\right\rVert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A7.E14Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E14Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathcal{O}\left(\left(\frac{\bar{r}L}{(1-\gamma)^{2}}+L_{\theta}\right)d^{\theta}\sqrt{\frac{\log(4M/\delta)}{M}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mi>θ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathcal{O}\left(\left(\frac{\bar{r}L}{(1-\gamma)^{2}}+L_{\theta}\right)d^{\theta}\sqrt{\frac{\log(4M/\delta)}{M}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A7.E14Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E14Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{(\bar{r}L+L_{\theta})d^{\theta}}{(1-\gamma)^{2}}\sqrt{\frac{\log(4M/\delta)}{M}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mi>θ</mi></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{(\bar{r}L+L_{\theta})d^{\theta}}{(1-\gamma)^{2}}\sqrt{\frac{\log(4M/\delta)}{M}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where the second inequality is due to Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma13" title="Lemma 13. ‣ Proof sketch of Theorem . ‣ G.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix G Missing proofs in Section ‣ Causality Meets Locality: Provably Generalizable and Scalable Policy Learning for Networked Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Putting all bounds together.</h5>

<div id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.2" class="ltx_p">With the above bounds on all <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{i}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{i}(k)</annotation></semantics></math>, we are now ready to prove the Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3 (Policy gradient convergence, informal). ‣ Actor convergence. ‣ 6.1 Convergence ‣ 6 Convergence results and adaptation gap ‣ Causality Meets Locality: Provably Generalizable and Scalable Policy Learning for Networked Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. Since <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla J(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla J(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz continuous, we have</p>
<table id="A7.E15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A7.E15X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E15X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle J(\theta(k+1))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J(\theta(k+1))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E15X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq J(\theta(k))+\langle\nabla J(\theta(k)),\theta(k+1)-\theta(k)\rangle-\frac{L^{\prime}}{2}\|\theta(k+1)-\theta(k)\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq J(\theta(k))+\langle\nabla J(\theta(k)),\theta(k+1)-\theta(k)\rangle-\frac{L^{\prime}}{2}\|\theta(k+1)-\theta(k)\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A7.E15Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E15Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=J(\theta(k))+\eta_{k}\langle\nabla J(\theta(k)),\hat{g}(k)\rangle-\frac{L^{\prime}\eta_{k}^{2}}{2}\|\hat{g}(k)\|^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=J(\theta(k))+\eta_{k}\langle\nabla J(\theta(k)),\hat{g}(k)\rangle-\frac{L^{\prime}\eta_{k}^{2}}{2}\|\hat{g}(k)\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Using the decomposition of <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{g}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{g}(k)</annotation></semantics></math> in Equation <a href="#A7.E12" title="In Proof sketch of Theorem . ‣ G.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix G Missing proofs in Section ‣ Causality Meets Locality: Provably Generalizable and Scalable Policy Learning for Networked Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>, we get,</p>
<table id="A7.Ex130" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex130.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\hat{g}(k)\|^{2}\leq 6\|e^{1}(k)\|^{2}+6\|e^{2}(k)\|^{2}+6\|e^{3}(k)\|^{2}+6\|e^{4}(k)\|^{2}+6\|e^{5}(k)\|^{2}+6\|\nabla J(\theta(k))\|^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\hat{g}(k)\|^{2}\leq 6\|e^{1}(k)\|^{2}+6\|e^{2}(k)\|^{2}+6\|e^{3}(k)\|^{2}+6\|e^{4}(k)\|^{2}+6\|e^{5}(k)\|^{2}+6\|\nabla J(\theta(k))\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.4" class="ltx_p">We bound <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\nabla J(\theta(k)),\hat{g}(k)\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\nabla J(\theta(k)),\hat{g}(k)\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> as follows</p>
<table id="A7.Ex131" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex131X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex131X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle\nabla J(\theta(k)),\hat{g}(k)\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle\nabla J(\theta(k)),\hat{g}(k)\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex131X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\|\nabla J(\theta(k))\|^{2}+\langle\nabla J(\theta(k)),\sum_{j=1}^{5}e^{j}(k)\rangle\geq\|\nabla J(\theta(k))\|^{2}+\langle\nabla J(\theta(k)),e^{2}(k)\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\|\nabla J(\theta(k))\|^{2}+\langle\nabla J(\theta(k)),\sum_{j=1}^{5}e^{j}(k)\rangle\geq\|\nabla J(\theta(k))\|^{2}+\langle\nabla J(\theta(k)),e^{2}(k)\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex131Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex131Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\|\nabla J(\theta(k))\|(\|e^{1}(k)\|+\|e^{3}(k)\|+\|e^{4}(k)\|+\|e^{5}(k)\|)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\|\nabla J(\theta(k))\|(\|e^{1}(k)\|+\|e^{3}(k)\|+\|e^{4}(k)\|+\|e^{5}(k)\|).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Plugging the above bounds on <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\hat{g}(k)\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\hat{g}(k)\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\nabla J(\theta(k)),\hat{g}(k)\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\nabla J(\theta(k)),\hat{g}(k)\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> into Equation <a href="#A7.E15" title="In Putting all bounds together. ‣ G.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix G Missing proofs in Section ‣ Causality Meets Locality: Provably Generalizable and Scalable Policy Learning for Networked Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>, we have</p>
<table id="A7.Ex132" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex132X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex132X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle J(\theta(k+1))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J(\theta(k+1))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex132X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq J(\theta(k))+(\eta_{k}-3L^{\prime}\eta_{k}^{2})\|\nabla J(\theta(k))\|^{2}+\eta_{k}\epsilon_{k,0}-\eta_{k}\epsilon_{k,1}-\eta_{k}^{2}\epsilon_{k,2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq J(\theta(k))+(\eta_{k}-3L^{\prime}\eta_{k}^{2})\|\nabla J(\theta(k))\|^{2}+\eta_{k}\epsilon_{k,0}-\eta_{k}\epsilon_{k,1}-\eta_{k}^{2}\epsilon_{k,2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.6" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{k,0}:=\langle\nabla J(\theta(k)),e^{2}(k)\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{k,0}:=\langle\nabla J(\theta(k)),e^{2}(k)\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{k,1}:=\|\nabla J(\theta(k))\|(\|e^{1}(k)\|+\|e^{3}(k)+\|e^{4}(k)+\|e^{5}(k)\|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0em">+</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{k,1}:=\|\nabla J(\theta(k))\|(\|e^{1}(k)\|+\|e^{3}(k)+\|e^{4}(k)+\|e^{5}(k)\|)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{k,2}:=3L^{\prime}\sum_{j=1}^{5}\|e^{j}(k)\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{k,2}:=3L^{\prime}\sum_{j=1}^{5}\|e^{j}(k)\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
It follows from telescoping sum that</p>
<table id="A7.Ex133" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex133X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex133X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle J(\theta(K))-J(\theta(0))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J(\theta(K))-J(\theta(0))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex133X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}(\eta_{k}-3L^{\prime}\eta_{k}^{2})\|\nabla J(\theta(k))\|^{2}+\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}\epsilon_{k,0}-\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}\epsilon_{k,1}-\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}^{2}\epsilon_{k,2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}(\eta_{k}-3L^{\prime}\eta_{k}^{2})\|\nabla J(\theta(k))\|^{2}+\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}\epsilon_{k,0}-\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}\epsilon_{k,1}-\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}^{2}\epsilon_{k,2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex133Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex133Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\frac{1}{2}\eta_{k}\|\nabla J(\theta(k))\|^{2}+\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}\epsilon_{k,0}-\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}\epsilon_{k,1}-\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}^{2}\epsilon_{k,2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\frac{1}{2}\eta_{k}\|\nabla J(\theta(k))\|^{2}+\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}\epsilon_{k,0}-\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}\epsilon_{k,1}-\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}^{2}\epsilon_{k,2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.7" class="ltx_p">where we use <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{k}-3L^{\prime}\eta_{k}^{2}=\eta_{k}(1-3L^{\prime}\eta_{k})\geq\tfrac{1}{2}\eta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{k}-3L^{\prime}\eta_{k}^{2}=\eta_{k}(1-3L^{\prime}\eta_{k})\geq\tfrac{1}{2}\eta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> given that <span id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;"> <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{k}\leq\tfrac{1}{6L^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">η</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">k</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">≤</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">1</mn><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">L</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">′</mo></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{k}\leq\tfrac{1}{6L^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> </span>.
After rearranging, we get</p>
<table id="A7.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\frac{1}{2}\eta_{k}\|\nabla J(\theta(k))\|^{2}\leq J(\theta(K))-J(\theta(0))-\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}\epsilon_{k,0}+\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}\epsilon_{k,1}+\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}^{2}\epsilon_{k,2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\frac{1}{2}\eta_{k}\|\nabla J(\theta(k))\|^{2}\leq J(\theta(K))-J(\theta(0))-\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}\epsilon_{k,0}+\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}\epsilon_{k,1}+\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}^{2}\epsilon_{k,2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.8" class="ltx_p">We now apply our bounds on each <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{j}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{j}(k)</annotation></semantics></math>. By Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma15" title="Lemma 15 (Adapted Lemma 15 []). ‣ Bounds on 𝑒^2⁢(𝑘). ‣ G.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix G Missing proofs in Section ‣ Causality Meets Locality: Provably Generalizable and Scalable Policy Learning for Networked Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>, we have with probability <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\tfrac{\delta}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\tfrac{\delta}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A7.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}\epsilon_{k,0}\leq\frac{2\bar{r}^{2}L^{2}}{(1-\gamma)^{4}}\sqrt{2\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}^{2}\log\frac{4}{\delta}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}\epsilon_{k,0}\leq\frac{2\bar{r}^{2}L^{2}}{(1-\gamma)^{4}}\sqrt{2\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}^{2}\log\frac{4}{\delta}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.9" class="ltx_p">By Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma14" title="Lemma 14 (Lemma 14, []). ‣ Bounds on 𝑒^1⁢(𝑘). ‣ G.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix G Missing proofs in Section ‣ Causality Meets Locality: Provably Generalizable and Scalable Policy Learning for Networked Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>, Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma16" title="Lemma 16 (Adapted Lemma 16, []). ‣ Bounds on 𝑒^3⁢(𝑘). ‣ G.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix G Missing proofs in Section ‣ Causality Meets Locality: Provably Generalizable and Scalable Policy Learning for Networked Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>, Equation <a href="#A7.E13" title="In Bounds on 𝑒^4⁢(𝑘). ‣ G.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix G Missing proofs in Section ‣ Causality Meets Locality: Provably Generalizable and Scalable Policy Learning for Networked Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a> and Equation <a href="#A7.E14" title="In Bounds on 𝑒^5⁢(𝑘). ‣ G.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix G Missing proofs in Section ‣ Causality Meets Locality: Provably Generalizable and Scalable Policy Learning for Networked Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>, we have with probability <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\tfrac{\delta}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\tfrac{\delta}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A7.E18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A7.E18X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E18X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sup_{k\leq K-1}\epsilon_{k,1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sup_{k\leq K-1}\epsilon_{k,1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E18X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{\bar{r}L}{(1-\gamma)^{2}}\left(\sup_{k\leq K-1}\|e^{1}(k)\|+\sup_{k\leq K-1}\|e^{3}(k)\|+\sup_{k\leq K-1}\|e^{4}(k)\|+\sup_{k\leq K-1}\|e^{5}(k)\|\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{\bar{r}L}{(1-\gamma)^{2}}\left(\sup_{k\leq K-1}\|e^{1}(k)\|+\sup_{k\leq K-1}\|e^{3}(k)\|+\sup_{k\leq K-1}\|e^{4}(k)\|+\sup_{k\leq K-1}\|e^{5}(k)\|\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A7.E18Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E18Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{\bar{r}L}{(1-\gamma)^{2}}\left(\frac{4cL\rho^{\kappa+1}}{(1-\gamma)^{3}}+2\frac{Lc}{(1-\gamma)}\rho^{\kappa+1}+L_{J}C_{\boldsymbol{\omega}}\sqrt{\frac{\log(4nM/\delta)}{T_{e}}}+C_{5}\frac{(\bar{r}L+L_{\theta})d^{\theta}}{(1-\gamma)^{2}}\sqrt{\frac{\log(4M/\delta)}{M}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>𝝎</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mi>θ</mi></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{\bar{r}L}{(1-\gamma)^{2}}\left(\frac{4cL\rho^{\kappa+1}}{(1-\gamma)^{3}}+2\frac{Lc}{(1-\gamma)}\rho^{\kappa+1}+L_{J}C_{\boldsymbol{\omega}}\sqrt{\frac{\log(4nM/\delta)}{T_{e}}}+C_{5}\frac{(\bar{r}L+L_{\theta})d^{\theta}}{(1-\gamma)^{2}}\sqrt{\frac{\log(4M/\delta)}{M}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A7.E18Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E18Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{6L^{2}c\bar{r}}{(1-\gamma)^{5}}\rho^{\kappa+1}+\frac{\bar{r}LL_{J}C_{\boldsymbol{\omega}}}{(1-\gamma)^{2}}\sqrt{\frac{\log(4nM/\delta)}{T_{e}}}+\frac{C_{5}(\bar{r}L+L_{\theta})d^{\theta}}{(1-\gamma)^{2}}\sqrt{\frac{\log(4M/\delta)}{M}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>5</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>𝝎</mi></msub></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mi>θ</mi></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{6L^{2}c\bar{r}}{(1-\gamma)^{5}}\rho^{\kappa+1}+\frac{\bar{r}LL_{J}C_{\boldsymbol{\omega}}}{(1-\gamma)^{2}}\sqrt{\frac{\log(4nM/\delta)}{T_{e}}}+\frac{C_{5}(\bar{r}L+L_{\theta})d^{\theta}}{(1-\gamma)^{2}}\sqrt{\frac{\log(4M/\delta)}{M}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.10" class="ltx_p">By Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma13" title="Lemma 13. ‣ Proof sketch of Theorem . ‣ G.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix G Missing proofs in Section ‣ Causality Meets Locality: Provably Generalizable and Scalable Policy Learning for Networked Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>, we have almost surely,</p>
<table id="A7.Ex134" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex134.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\max_{1\leq j\leq 5}(\|e^{j}(k)\|\|)\leq 2\tfrac{\bar{r}L}{(1-\gamma)^{2}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{1\leq j\leq 5}(\|e^{j}(k)\|\|)\leq 2\tfrac{\bar{r}L}{(1-\gamma)^{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.11" class="ltx_p">and hence,</p>
<table id="A7.Ex135" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex135.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{k\leq K-1}\epsilon_{k,2}=3L^{\prime}\sum_{j=1}^{5}\|e^{j}(m)\|^{2}\leq\frac{60\bar{r}^{2}L^{\prime}L^{2}}{(1-\gamma)^{4}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></munderover><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>60</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{k\leq K-1}\epsilon_{k,2}=3L^{\prime}\sum_{j=1}^{5}\|e^{j}(m)\|^{2}\leq\frac{60\bar{r}^{2}L^{\prime}L^{2}}{(1-\gamma)^{4}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.12" class="ltx_p">Using a union bound, we have with probability <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, all three events hold, thus</p>
<table id="A7.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex136"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex136.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}\|\nabla J(\theta(k))\|^{2}}{\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}\|\nabla J(\theta(k))\|^{2}}{\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex137"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex137.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{2(J(\theta(K))-J(\theta(0)))+2\left|\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}\epsilon_{k,0}\right|+2\sup_{k}\epsilon_{k,2}\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}^{2}}{\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}}+2\sup_{k}\epsilon_{k,1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mi>k</mi></munder><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{2(J(\theta(K))-J(\theta(0)))+2\left|\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}\epsilon_{k,0}\right|+2\sup_{k}\epsilon_{k,2}\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}^{2}}{\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}}+2\sup_{k}\epsilon_{k,1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex138"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex138.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{2(J(\theta(K))-J(\theta(0)))+\dfrac{4\bar{r}^{2}L^{2}}{(1-\gamma)^{4}}\sqrt{2\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}^{2}\log\dfrac{4}{\delta}}+\dfrac{120\bar{r}^{2}L^{\prime}L^{2}}{(1-\gamma)^{4}}\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}^{2}}{\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>120</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{2(J(\theta(K))-J(\theta(0)))+\dfrac{4\bar{r}^{2}L^{2}}{(1-\gamma)^{4}}\sqrt{2\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}^{2}\log\dfrac{4}{\delta}}+\dfrac{120\bar{r}^{2}L^{\prime}L^{2}}{(1-\gamma)^{4}}\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}^{2}}{\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex139"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex139.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{12L^{2}c\bar{r}}{(1-\gamma)^{5}}\rho^{\kappa+1}+\frac{2\bar{r}LL_{J}C_{\boldsymbol{\omega}}}{(1-\gamma)^{2}}\sqrt{\frac{\log(4nM/\delta)}{T_{e}}}+\frac{2C_{5}(\bar{r}L+L_{\theta})d^{\theta}}{(1-\gamma)^{2}}\sqrt{\frac{\log(4M/\delta)}{M}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>5</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>𝝎</mi></msub></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mi>θ</mi></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{12L^{2}c\bar{r}}{(1-\gamma)^{5}}\rho^{\kappa+1}+\frac{2\bar{r}LL_{J}C_{\boldsymbol{\omega}}}{(1-\gamma)^{2}}\sqrt{\frac{\log(4nM/\delta)}{T_{e}}}+\frac{2C_{5}(\bar{r}L+L_{\theta})d^{\theta}}{(1-\gamma)^{2}}\sqrt{\frac{\log(4M/\delta)}{M}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.13" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{k}=\dfrac{\eta}{\sqrt{k+1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>η</mi><msqrt><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{k}=\dfrac{\eta}{\sqrt{k+1}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A7.Ex140" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex140.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}&gt;2\eta(\sqrt{K+1}-1)\geq\eta\sqrt{K+1}\quad\text{and}\quad\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}^{2}&lt;\eta^{2}(1+\log K)&lt;2\eta^{2}\log K\quad(\text{using }K\geq 3)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>using </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}&gt;2\eta(\sqrt{K+1}-1)\geq\eta\sqrt{K+1}\quad\text{and}\quad\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}^{2}&lt;\eta^{2}(1+\log K)&lt;2\eta^{2}\log K\quad(\text{using }K\geq 3).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.14" class="ltx_p">Further we use the bound <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\theta(K))\leq\dfrac{\bar{r}}{1-\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\theta(K))\leq\dfrac{\bar{r}}{1-\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\theta(0))\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\theta(0))\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> almost surely. Combining these results, we get with probability <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A7.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex141"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex141.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}\|\nabla J(\theta(k))\|^{2}}{\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}}\leq\frac{\frac{2\bar{r}}{\eta(1-\gamma)}+\frac{8\bar{r}^{2}L^{2}}{(1-\gamma)^{4}}\sqrt{\log K\log\dfrac{4}{\delta}}+\frac{240\bar{r}^{2}L^{\prime}L^{2}}{(1-\gamma)^{4}}\eta\log K}{\sqrt{K+1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>240</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}\|\nabla J(\theta(k))\|^{2}}{\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}}\leq\frac{\frac{2\bar{r}}{\eta(1-\gamma)}+\frac{8\bar{r}^{2}L^{2}}{(1-\gamma)^{4}}\sqrt{\log K\log\dfrac{4}{\delta}}+\frac{240\bar{r}^{2}L^{\prime}L^{2}}{(1-\gamma)^{4}}\eta\log K}{\sqrt{K+1}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex142"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex142.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{12L^{2}c\bar{r}}{(1-\gamma)^{5}}\rho^{\kappa+1}+\frac{2\bar{r}LL_{J}C_{\boldsymbol{\omega}}}{(1-\gamma)^{2}}\sqrt{\frac{\log(4nM/\delta)}{T_{e}}}+\frac{2C_{5}(\bar{r}L+L_{\theta})d^{\theta}}{(1-\gamma)^{2}}\sqrt{\frac{\log(4M/\delta)}{M}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>5</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>𝝎</mi></msub></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mi>θ</mi></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{12L^{2}c\bar{r}}{(1-\gamma)^{5}}\rho^{\kappa+1}+\frac{2\bar{r}LL_{J}C_{\boldsymbol{\omega}}}{(1-\gamma)^{2}}\sqrt{\frac{\log(4nM/\delta)}{T_{e}}}+\frac{2C_{5}(\bar{r}L+L_{\theta})d^{\theta}}{(1-\gamma)^{2}}\sqrt{\frac{\log(4M/\delta)}{M}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.15" class="ltx_p">∎</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS3.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">G.3.1 </span>Empirical convergence</h4>

<div id="Thmcorollary4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmcorollary4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 4</span></span><span id="Thmcorollary4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Empirical convergence)<span id="Thmcorollary4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmcorollary4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmcorollary4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Under the same setup of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3 (Policy gradient convergence, informal). ‣ Actor convergence. ‣ 6.1 Convergence ‣ 6 Convergence results and adaptation gap ‣ Causality Meets Locality: Provably Generalizable and Scalable Policy Learning for Networked Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, with probability at least <math id="Thmcorollary4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, when domain factors are estimated with <math id="Thmcorollary4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{e}</annotation></semantics></math> trajectories:</p>
<table id="A7.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex143"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex143.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}\|\nabla J(\theta(k),\mathcal{D}^{M})\|^{2}}{\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>M</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}\|\nabla J(\theta(k),\mathcal{D}^{M})\|^{2}}{\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex143.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{\frac{2\bar{r}}{\eta(1-\gamma)}+\frac{8\bar{r}^{2}L^{2}}{(1-\gamma)^{4}}\sqrt{\log K\log\dfrac{4}{\delta}}+\frac{240\bar{r}^{2}L^{\prime}L^{2}}{(1-\gamma)^{4}}\eta\log K}{\sqrt{K+1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>240</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{\frac{2\bar{r}}{\eta(1-\gamma)}+\frac{8\bar{r}^{2}L^{2}}{(1-\gamma)^{4}}\sqrt{\log K\log\dfrac{4}{\delta}}+\frac{240\bar{r}^{2}L^{\prime}L^{2}}{(1-\gamma)^{4}}\eta\log K}{\sqrt{K+1}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex144"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex144.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{12L^{2}c\bar{r}}{(1-\gamma)^{5}}\rho^{\kappa+1}+\frac{2\bar{r}LL_{J}C_{\boldsymbol{\omega}}}{(1-\gamma)^{2}}\sqrt{\frac{\log(4nM/\delta)}{T_{e}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>5</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>𝝎</mi></msub></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{12L^{2}c\bar{r}}{(1-\gamma)^{5}}\rho^{\kappa+1}+\frac{2\bar{r}LL_{J}C_{\boldsymbol{\omega}}}{(1-\gamma)^{2}}\sqrt{\frac{\log(4nM/\delta)}{T_{e}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex145"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex145.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}\|\nabla J(\theta(k),\hat{\mathcal{D}}^{M})\|^{2}}{\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>M</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}\|\nabla J(\theta(k),\hat{\mathcal{D}}^{M})\|^{2}}{\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\eta_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex145.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{\frac{2\bar{r}}{\eta(1-\gamma)}+\frac{8\bar{r}^{2}L^{2}}{(1-\gamma)^{4}}\sqrt{\log K\log\dfrac{4}{\delta}}+\frac{240\bar{r}^{2}L^{\prime}L^{2}}{(1-\gamma)^{4}}\eta\log K}{\sqrt{K+1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>240</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{\frac{2\bar{r}}{\eta(1-\gamma)}+\frac{8\bar{r}^{2}L^{2}}{(1-\gamma)^{4}}\sqrt{\log K\log\dfrac{4}{\delta}}+\frac{240\bar{r}^{2}L^{\prime}L^{2}}{(1-\gamma)^{4}}\eta\log K}{\sqrt{K+1}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex146"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex146.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{12L^{2}c\bar{r}}{(1-\gamma)^{5}}\rho^{\kappa+1}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>5</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{12L^{2}c\bar{r}}{(1-\gamma)^{5}}\rho^{\kappa+1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.4 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4 (Adaptation guarantee). ‣ 6.2 Generalization ‣ 6 Convergence results and adaptation gap ‣ Causality Meets Locality: Provably Generalizable and Scalable Policy Learning for Networked Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></h3>

<div id="A7.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A7.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">We use the Lipschitz continuity of <math id="A7.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\theta,\boldsymbol{\omega}^{\prime};\boldsymbol{\omega})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\theta,\boldsymbol{\omega}^{\prime};\boldsymbol{\omega})</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="A7.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\omega}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\omega}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex147"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex147.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle J(\theta(K),\hat{\boldsymbol{\omega}}^{M+1};\boldsymbol{\omega}^{M+1})-J(\theta(K),\boldsymbol{\omega}^{M+1};\boldsymbol{\omega}^{M+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝝎</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝝎</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝝎</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J(\theta(K),\hat{\boldsymbol{\omega}}^{M+1};\boldsymbol{\omega}^{M+1})-J(\theta(K),\boldsymbol{\omega}^{M+1};\boldsymbol{\omega}^{M+1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex147.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq-L_{\boldsymbol{\omega}^{\prime}}\left\lVert\hat{\boldsymbol{\omega}}^{M+1}-\boldsymbol{\omega}^{M+1}\right\rVert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><msup><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝝎</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq-L_{\boldsymbol{\omega}^{\prime}}\left\lVert\hat{\boldsymbol{\omega}}^{M+1}-\boldsymbol{\omega}^{M+1}\right\rVert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex148"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex148.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq-L_{\boldsymbol{\omega}^{\prime}}C_{\boldsymbol{\omega}}\sqrt{\frac{\log(n/\delta)}{T_{a}}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><msup><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>𝝎</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq-L_{\boldsymbol{\omega}^{\prime}}C_{\boldsymbol{\omega}}\sqrt{\frac{\log(n/\delta)}{T_{a}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">It follows that</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex149"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex149.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[J(\theta(K),\hat{\boldsymbol{\omega}}^{M+1};\boldsymbol{\omega}^{M+1})|\theta(K)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝝎</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[J(\theta(K),\hat{\boldsymbol{\omega}}^{M+1};\boldsymbol{\omega}^{M+1})|\theta(K)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex149.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\mathbb{E}\left[J(\theta(K),\boldsymbol{\omega}^{M+1})|\theta(K)\right]-L_{\boldsymbol{\omega}^{\prime}}C_{\boldsymbol{\omega}}\sqrt{\frac{\log(n/\delta)}{T_{a}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝝎</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><msup><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>𝝎</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\mathbb{E}\left[J(\theta(K),\boldsymbol{\omega}^{M+1})|\theta(K)\right]-L_{\boldsymbol{\omega}^{\prime}}C_{\boldsymbol{\omega}}\sqrt{\frac{\log(n/\delta)}{T_{a}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex150"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex150.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=J(\theta(K))-L_{\boldsymbol{\omega}^{\prime}}C_{\boldsymbol{\omega}}\sqrt{\frac{\log(n/\delta)}{T_{a}}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><msup><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>𝝎</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=J(\theta(K))-L_{\boldsymbol{\omega}^{\prime}}C_{\boldsymbol{\omega}}\sqrt{\frac{\log(n/\delta)}{T_{a}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS4.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS4.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A8" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix H </span>Comprehensive Experiments</h2>

<div id="A8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We begin by clarifying the distinction between the <em id="A8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">meta-RL</em> and <em id="A8.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">multi-task RL</em> paradigms to highlight the key differences between our algorithmic design and baseline methods.</p>
</div>
<section id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Clarification: Meta-RL vs. Multi-task RL</h5>

<div id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The goal of multi-task RL <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>]</cite> is to learn a single task-conditioned policy that maximizes the average expected return across all source domains drawn from a domain distribution. However, multi-task RL does not provide any guarantee of rapid few-shot adaptation to new, unseen domains. In contrast, meta-RL explicitly aims to <em id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">learn to adapt</em>: it leverages the set of source domains to train a policy that can be efficiently adapted to a new domain using only a small number of trajectories at test time.</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore, <span id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">GSAC</span> falls under the meta-RL framework. Our objective is to achieve fast adaptation in a new domain with limited data. Specifically, we train a shared, domain-factor-conditioned policy across source domains and, during adaptation, estimate the domain factors <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\omega}</annotation></semantics></math> from only a few trajectories to enable immediate policy deployment without additional fine-tuning.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">H.1 </span>Wireless communication</h3>

<section id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Environment setup.</h5>

<div id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The network consists of <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> users positioned on a 2D grid. Each user maintains a queue of packets with a fixed deadline <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}=2</annotation></semantics></math>. At every timestep, a new packet arrives at user <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> with probability <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}\sim\text{Unif}[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext>Unif</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}\sim\text{Unif}[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. The user either transmits the earliest packet to a randomly selected access point (AP) <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}(t)\in Y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}(t)\in Y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, or remains idle. A transmission to AP <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> succeeds with probability <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}\sim\text{Unif}[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext>Unif</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}\sim\text{Unif}[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> if no other user simultaneously transmits to the same AP; otherwise, a collision occurs and no transmission succeeds. Each successful transmission yields a reward of 1.</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The local state of each user <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}_{i}(t)=(b_{i,1}(t),\ldots,b_{i,d_{i}}(t),z_{i,1}(t),z_{i,2}(t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}_{i}(t)=(b_{i,1}(t),\ldots,b_{i,d_{i}}(t),z_{i,1}(t),z_{i,2}(t))</annotation></semantics></math>. <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{i}(t)\in\{0,1\}^{d_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{i}(t)\in\{0,1\}^{d_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> encodes queue status by deadline bins (e.g., <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{i}(t)=(1,1,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{i}(t)=(1,1,0)</annotation></semantics></math> means the first two deadline bins are occupied while the third is empty). <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i,1}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i,1}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i,2}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i,2}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> are irrelevant components to decision quality. <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i,1}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i,1}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is the channel quality indicator, which does not influence the packet success probability <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, as <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> depends solely on collisions. <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i,2}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i,2}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is the grid coordinates, which adds no useful information because the connectivity graph already encodes all relevant interactions.</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The action space is <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{i}=Y_{i}\cup\{\texttt{null}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">null</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{i}=Y_{i}\cup\{\texttt{null}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <span id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">null</span> denotes the idle action. The interaction graph is defined by overlapping access point sets: two users are neighbors if they share at least one AP. This induces local dependencies, which define each agent’s <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>-hop neighborhood for state, action, and domain-factor inputs.</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A8.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ Domain shift sensitivity. ‣ H.1 Wireless communication ‣ Appendix H Comprehensive Experiments ‣ Causality Meets Locality: Provably Generalizable and Scalable Policy Learning for Networked Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> visualizes the communication graph induced by different grid sizes: <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\times 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\times 3</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4\times 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\times 4</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\times 5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\times 5</annotation></semantics></math>. Each user is placed at a grid cell and is connected to APs located at the corners of grid blocks. Users that share an AP form communication links, resulting in a structured interaction graph. This setup highlights the challenge of scalability in networked MARL, as larger grids yield significantly higher local complexity and increased neighborhood sizes. Figure <a href="#A8.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ Domain shift sensitivity. ‣ H.1 Wireless communication ‣ Appendix H Comprehensive Experiments ‣ Causality Meets Locality: Provably Generalizable and Scalable Policy Learning for Networked Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> illustrates the local neighborhood (i.e., <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>-hop graph connectivity) for a representative agent in each grid size. These visualizations demonstrate how local dependencies expand with increasing grid sizes. The number of neighbors within <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa=1</annotation></semantics></math> grows with the grid size, resulting in higher-dimensional input spaces for both state and domain-factor features.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Benefits of ACR.</h5>

<div id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The ACR procedure automatically prunes such irrelevant or redundant variables, retaining only those that causally influence the local reward or dynamics. This yields a non-trivial reduction in local dimensionality. For example, consider a <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4\times 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\times 4</annotation></semantics></math> grid with <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}=2</annotation></semantics></math> and a neighborhood size <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|N_{i}|=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|N_{i}|=5</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<ul id="A8.I1" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A8.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A8.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Raw (truncation-only): <math id="A8.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|N_{i}|\times(d_{i}+2)=5\times 4=20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|N_{i}|\times(d_{i}+2)=5\times 4=20</annotation></semantics></math> features.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A8.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A8.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">With ACR: <math id="A8.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|N_{i}|\times d_{i}=5\times 2=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|N_{i}|\times d_{i}=5\times 2=10</annotation></semantics></math> features.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This 50% shrinkage directly translates into:</p>
<ul id="A8.I2" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A8.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A8.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Smaller critics and lower compute: reduced local state–action support and table size.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A8.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A8.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Faster learning: lower variance in actor updates and tighter constants in our bounds.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A8.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A8.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Accuracy preserved: approximation error remains controlled (see Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1 (Approximation error of value ACR). ‣ 3.1 ACR for fixed environment ‣ 3 Approximately compact representation ‣ Causality Meets Locality: Provably Generalizable and Scalable Policy Learning for Networked Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>-<a href="#Thmproposition2" title="Proposition 2 (Approximation error). ‣ 3.1 ACR for fixed environment ‣ 3 Approximately compact representation ‣ Causality Meets Locality: Provably Generalizable and Scalable Policy Learning for Networked Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A8.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A8.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Improved sample efficiency: by effectively increasing the minimum visitation <math id="A8.I2.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> and reducing the mixing constant <math id="A8.I2.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> (Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2. ‣ 6.1 Convergence ‣ 6 Convergence results and adaptation gap ‣ Causality Meets Locality: Provably Generalizable and Scalable Policy Learning for Networked Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), ACRs tighten the constants in the convergence guarantee (Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Critic error bound, informal). ‣ Critic error bound. ‣ 6.1 Convergence ‣ 6 Convergence results and adaptation gap ‣ Causality Meets Locality: Provably Generalizable and Scalable Policy Learning for Networked Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evaluation protocol.</h5>

<div id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We generate <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=3</annotation></semantics></math> source domains by sampling domain factors <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{0.2,0.5,0.8\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0.2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.8</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0.2,0.5,0.8\}</annotation></semantics></math>, while the target domain uses <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\text{target}}=0.65" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.65</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\text{target}}=0.65</annotation></semantics></math> unless otherwise specified. In each domain, <span id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">GSAC</span> is trained for <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> outer iterations (variable depending on convergence), with a time horizon of <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=10</annotation></semantics></math>. We use a constant stepsize of <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0.1</annotation></semantics></math> for the critic and <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=0.01</annotation></semantics></math> for the actor. The softmax temperature is set to <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>, and the discount factor is <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=0.95" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.95</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=0.95</annotation></semantics></math>. For domain factor estimation, we collect <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{e}=20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{e}=20</annotation></semantics></math> trajectories per domain. To evaluate adaptation in the target domain, we compare our algorithm against three baselines: <span id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">SAC-MTL</span>, <span id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">SAC-FT</span>, <span id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">SAC-LFS</span>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Domain shift sensitivity.</h5>

<div id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To assess generalization under varying domain factors, we vary the target packet arrival rate with <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\text{target}}\in\{0.6,0.65,0.7\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0.6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.65</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.7</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\text{target}}\in\{0.6,0.65,0.7\}</annotation></semantics></math>. As shown in Figure <a href="#A8.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ Domain shift sensitivity. ‣ H.1 Wireless communication ‣ Appendix H Comprehensive Experiments ‣ Causality Meets Locality: Provably Generalizable and Scalable Policy Learning for Networked Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, <span id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">GSAC</span> consistently adapts to new domain settings with minimal performance degradation, even when the target domain differs significantly from the training domains. Notably, it outperforms all three baselines across all configurations. Moreover, Figures <a href="#S7.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 7 Numerical experiments ‣ Causality Meets Locality: Provably Generalizable and Scalable Policy Learning for Networked Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and <a href="#A8.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ Domain shift sensitivity. ‣ H.1 Wireless communication ‣ Appendix H Comprehensive Experiments ‣ Causality Meets Locality: Provably Generalizable and Scalable Policy Learning for Networked Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> demonstrate that <span id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">GSAC</span> can rapidly adapt to new environments using only a few trajectories.</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Across all settings, <span id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">GSAC</span> demonstrates: (i) consistent improvement over training iterations; (ii) fast adaptation from a few trajectories; and (iii) robust performance under domain shifts. These findings support our theoretical claims on scalability and generalizability in large-scale networked MARL systems.</p>
</div>
