<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A8.F7.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span><math id="A8.F7.sf2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\text{target}}=0.65" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">p</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">target</mtext></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0.65</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\text{target}}=0.65</annotation></semantics></math></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="A8.F7.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.21427v1/figures/p3_GS3_TP0.7.png" id="A8.F7.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/286;" width="476" height="286" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A8.F7.sf3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(c)</span> </span><math id="A8.F7.sf3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\text{target}}=0.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">p</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">target</mtext></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0.7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\text{target}}=0.7</annotation></semantics></math></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A8.F7.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 7</span>: </span><span id="A8.F7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Adaptation comparison for different target domains in wireless communication benchmark.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">H.2 </span>Traffic control</h3>

<section id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Environment setup.</h5>

<div id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The environment consists of a network of <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> interconnected road links forming a directed graph. Each node <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> represents a road link, and the edges define feasible turning movements between links. The local state of link <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is denoted by <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}_{i}(t)=(x_{ij}(t))_{j\in\mathcal{N}_{i}^{\text{out}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>out</mtext></msubsup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}_{i}(t)=(x_{ij}(t))_{j\in\mathcal{N}_{i}^{\text{out}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{ij}(t)\in[S]=\{0,1,\dots,S\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{ij}(t)\in[S]=\{0,1,\dots,S\}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the number of vehicles on link <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> intending to turn to neighboring link <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>. Accordingly, the local state space is <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{i}=[S]^{|\mathcal{N}_{i}^{\text{out}}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>out</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{i}=[S]^{|\mathcal{N}_{i}^{\text{out}}|}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The local action <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}(t)=(y_{ij}(t))_{j\in\mathcal{N}_{i}^{\text{out}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>out</mtext></msubsup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}(t)=(y_{ij}(t))_{j\in\mathcal{N}_{i}^{\text{out}}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a binary traffic-signal tuple, where <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{ij}(t)\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{ij}(t)\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> controls whether the turn movement <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i\to j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i\to j)</annotation></semantics></math> is allowed at time <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, the local action space is <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{i}=\{0,1\}^{|\mathcal{N}_{i}^{\text{out}}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>out</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{i}=\{0,1\}^{|\mathcal{N}_{i}^{\text{out}}|}</annotation></semantics></math>. When <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{ij}(t)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{ij}(t)=1</annotation></semantics></math>, a random number of queued vehicles <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{ij}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{ij}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> will depart link <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and flow into link <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>, subject to capacity and queue constraints. Meanwhile, link <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> receives incoming flows from other connected links <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\mathcal{N}_{i}^{\text{in}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>in</mtext></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\mathcal{N}_{i}^{\text{in}}</annotation></semantics></math>, where a random fraction <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{ij}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{ij}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> of the inflow is assigned to each downstream queue <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{ij}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{ij}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>. The resulting dynamics are</p>
<table id="A8.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{ij}(t+1)=[x_{ij}(t)-\min(C_{ij}(t)y_{ij}(t),x_{ij}(t))]_{0}^{S}+\sum_{k\in\mathcal{N}_{i}^{\text{in}}}\min(C_{ki}(t)y_{ki}(t),x_{ki}(t))R_{ij}(t)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>0</mn><mi>S</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>in</mtext></msubsup></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{ij}(t+1)=[x_{ij}(t)-\min(C_{ij}(t)y_{ij}(t),x_{ij}(t))]_{0}^{S}+\sum_{k\in\mathcal{N}_{i}^{\text{in}}}\min(C_{ki}(t)y_{ki}(t),x_{ki}(t))R_{ij}(t),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[x]_{0}^{S}=\max(\min(x,S),0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>0</mn><mi>S</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[x]_{0}^{S}=\max(\min(x,S),0)</annotation></semantics></math>. The random variables <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{ij}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{ij}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{ij}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{ij}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> are drawn i.i.d. from fixed distributions, defining stochastic yet locally dependent transitions. This structure ensures that <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}_{i}(t+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}_{i}(t+1)</annotation></semantics></math> depends only on the states and actions within link <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>’s neighborhood, consistent with the local interaction model in Section 2.1.</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The local reward is defined as the negative queue length, quantifying congestion at each link:</p>
<table id="A8.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="r_{i}(\mathbf{s}_{i},a_{i})=-\sum_{j\in\mathcal{N}_{i}^{\text{out}}}x_{ij}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>out</mtext></msubsup></mrow></munder><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}(\mathbf{s}_{i},a_{i})=-\sum_{j\in\mathcal{N}_{i}^{\text{out}}}x_{ij}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Intuitively, the objective is to minimize network-wide congestion by controlling local signals. Policies such as the max-pressure controller typically rely on known traffic-flow statistics, while our learning framework operates in a model-free fashion, adapting from observed data without prior knowledge of <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> distributions.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evaluation protocol.</h5>

<div id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate performance under <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=3</annotation></semantics></math> source domains, each defined by different vehicle flow intensities sampled from <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\text{low},\text{medium},\text{high}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mtext>low</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext>medium</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext>high</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\text{low},\text{medium},\text{high}\}</annotation></semantics></math> levels of <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{ij}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{ij}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>. The target domain adopts an intermediate traffic level unless otherwise stated. Each experiment runs for <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=50</annotation></semantics></math> timesteps, with discount factor <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=0.95" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.95</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=0.95</annotation></semantics></math> and learning rates <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0.1</annotation></semantics></math> for the critic and <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=0.01</annotation></semantics></math> for the actor. For domain factor estimation, <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{e}=20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{e}=20</annotation></semantics></math> trajectories are collected per domain.</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To assess adaptation, we compare <span id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">GSAC</span> against a <span id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">SAC-LFS</span> baseline trained directly in the target domain. We also vary the network topology by adjusting the number of intersections <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in\{9,16,25\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>25</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in\{9,16,25\}</annotation></semantics></math>, corresponding to <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\times 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\times 3</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4\times 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\times 4</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\times 5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\times 5</annotation></semantics></math> grid layouts. As is shown in Figure <a href="#A8.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ Evaluation protocol. ‣ H.2 Traffic control ‣ Appendix H Comprehensive Experiments ‣ Causality Meets Locality: Provably Generalizable and Scalable Policy Learning for Networked Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>, <span id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">GSAC</span> achieves faster adaptation, lower queue lengths, and improved stability across all configurations.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A8.F8" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="A8.F8.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.21427v1/figures/gridsize_3_comparison.png" id="A8.F8.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/374;" width="476" height="374" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A8.F8.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><span id="A8.F8.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">grid size 3</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="A8.F8.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.21427v1/figures/gridsize_4_comparison.png" id="A8.F8.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/374;" width="476" height="374" alt="Refer to caption">
